{{- define "collective-plan-scoping" -}}
{{- $hasGraph := or (gt (len .TaskGraph.DirectDependencies) 0) (gt (len .TaskGraph.BlockedRelatedTasks) 0) (gt (len .TaskGraph.SiblingsSharingRefs) 0) (gt (len .TaskGraph.CompletedArtifacts) 0) -}}
{{- if or (gt .TotalPlanTasks 1) $hasGraph}}

=== COLLECTIVE PLAN SCOPING ===
{{template "artifact-ref-fallback" .}}
{{- if gt .TotalPlanTasks 1}}
This task is {{.TaskOrdinal}} of {{.TotalPlanTasks}} in the current sprint plan.
Read the full goal spec ({{.GoalSpecRef}}) to understand {{- if eq .RoleType "reviewer"}} the complete picture.
Verify {{- if eq .Role "us-reviewer"}} stories stay within scope — flag Scope Absorption into sibling territory.{{- else if eq .Role "code-plan-reviewer"}} the plan stays within scope — flag scope creep into sibling territory.{{- else if eq .Role "epic-plan-reviewer"}} the epic stays within scope — flag scope creep into sibling territory.{{- else}} the implementation stays within scope — flag scope creep as a blocker.{{- end}}
{{- else}} how your work integrates.
Your scope is LIMITED to what is described in SCOPE above.
{{- if eq .Role "us-writer"}}
Do NOT write stories that belong to a sibling task's scope — this is Scope Absorption.
{{- else if eq .Role "code-planner"}}
Do NOT plan work that belongs to a sibling task's scope.
{{- else if eq .Role "epic-planner"}}
Do NOT plan capabilities that belong to a sibling task's scope.
{{- else}}
If you must modify a file outside your scope, declare it in scope_extensions with justification.
Do NOT silently modify out-of-scope files — undeclared scope changes will be rejected.
If you discover work needed outside your scope that you cannot handle, log it as a spec_gap anomaly.
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

RELEVANT TASK GRAPH DIGEST:
Use this compact digest before broad state queries. Active tasks: `liza get tasks --active --summary --json`.
{{- if gt (len .TaskGraph.DirectDependencies) 0}}
Direct dependencies:
{{- range .TaskGraph.DirectDependencies}}
{{template "task-graph-entry" .}}
{{- end}}
{{- else}}
Direct dependencies: none listed.
{{- end}}
{{- if gt (len .TaskGraph.BlockedRelatedTasks) 0}}

Blocked related tasks:
{{- range .TaskGraph.BlockedRelatedTasks}}
{{template "task-graph-entry" .}}
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- if gt (len .TaskGraph.SiblingsSharingRefs) 0}}

Siblings with overlapping file refs:
{{- range .TaskGraph.SiblingsSharingRefs}}
{{template "task-graph-entry" .}}
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- if gt (len .TaskGraph.CompletedArtifacts) 0}}

Completed artifacts:
{{- range .TaskGraph.CompletedArtifacts}}
{{template "task-graph-entry" .}}
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- if gt .TotalPlanTasks 1}}

Plan siblings (scope boundary only):
{{- range .SiblingTasks}}
- {{.ID}} [{{.Status}}]: {{.Description}} | task detail: liza get {{.ID}} --json
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- if ne .PlanRef ""}}
PLAN ARTIFACT: {{.PlanRef}}
{{- end}}
{{- /* Sibling-consistency rule: rendered when task depends on same-role-pair phase dependencies */ -}}
{{- if .PhaseDependencyTasks}}

SIBLING CONSISTENCY RULE:
This task depends on prior planning task(s):
{{- range .PhaseDependencyTasks}}
- {{.ID}} [{{.Status}}]{{if ne .PlanRef ""}} — plan: {{.PlanRef}}{{end}}
{{- end}}
If your plan CANNOT be made consistent with those prior plans:
- Do NOT iterate with the reviewer — mark BLOCKED immediately via liza mark-blocked --json.
- blocked_reason: which prior task constraint conflicts and why.
- blocked_questions: what needs to change in prior plans to resolve.
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "task-graph-entry" -}}
- {{.ID}} [{{.Status}}]: {{.Description}} | task detail: liza get {{.ID}} --json{{if .OutputRefs}} | produced outputs: liza get {{.ID}} --output-summary --json{{end -}}
{{- if .BlockedReason}} | blocker: {{.BlockedReason}}{{end -}}
{{- if .RepairOperation}} | repair: {{.RepairOperation}}{{end}}
{{- end -}}
